# Architecture: which rules apply to which path

`AGENTS.md` holds the rules every file obeys. This page narrows them per path so
an agent editing one file does not have to read every document.

The table is the source of truth for **where** a rule applies. For **what** the
rule is, follow the linked document; when the two disagree, the document wins and
this table is fixed in the same change.

## Which rules apply to this path

| Path | Read before editing | Extra rules that apply only here |
|---|---|---|
{% if backend %}
| `{{ backend_root }}/app/core/` | [backend.md](backend.md), [security.md](security.md) | Config comes from settings only; no `os.environ` reads elsewhere; secrets typed as secret fields |
| `{{ backend_root }}/app/modules/*/router.py` | [backend.md](backend.md) | Every route declares its response type, status code, and permission; request schemas reject unknown fields; the router holds no business rules |
| `{{ backend_root }}/app/modules/*/service.py` | [backend.md](backend.md) | Owns the transaction boundary; no web-framework imports; raises typed domain errors |
| `{{ backend_root }}/app/modules/*/repository.py` | [backend.md](backend.md), [database.md](database.md) | Holds every data-store call for the module; never commits; always filters by tenant |
| `{{ backend_root }}/app/modules/*/models.py` | [database.md](database.md) | Present only if the project uses an ORM; no business logic; never returned from a router |
| `{{ backend_root }}/app/modules/*/tasks.py` | [backend.md](backend.md) | Idempotent, bounded retries, time limits, small payloads (IDs only) |
| `{{ migrations_root }}/` | [database.md](database.md) | Forward-only; never edit an applied migration; expand/contract |
{% endif %}
{% if frontend %}
| `{{ frontend_root }}/src/app/` | [frontend.md](frontend.md) | Layer `app` only wires things; route adapters contain imports and re-exports, no markup or copy |
| `{{ frontend_root }}/src/pages/*/model/content.ts` | [frontend.md](frontend.md) | Page copy lives here, not in JSX |
| `{{ frontend_root }}/src/shared/ui/` | [frontend.md](frontend.md), [security.md](security.md) | Business-agnostic only; no data fetching; accessible primitives land here |
| `{{ frontend_root }}/src/shared/api/` | [frontend.md](frontend.md) | Generated types only; the typed client, auth header injection, and error mapping live here |
| `eslint.config.mjs`, `docs/architecture/frontend.verify.mjs` | [frontend.md](frontend.md) | The two FSD rule sets must agree; changing a boundary rule requires an ADR |
{% endif %}
| `docs/product/business-rules.md` | — | A rule change needs the rule owner's approval; IDs are stable |
| `docs/architecture/decisions/` | `decisions/000-template.md` | Decided ADRs are never edited; supersede with a new one |
| `AGENTS.md`, this file | — | A rule change here is an architecture change: say why in the PR, and keep every command verifiable |

## Adding a path

Add a row when a path has a rule that does not apply repository-wide, or when it
is edited often enough that "read everything first" is too expensive. Every row
must link to a document that exists; a row pointing at a missing file is a bug.

An agent that finds its path is **not** in this table follows `AGENTS.md` only,
and says so rather than inventing a rule.
